	(footprint "USB_C_Plug_XUNPU_TYPEC-950-ARP24"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "3ad5e5d3-ec68-599e-bf4f-fd2b55b4509f")
		(at 100 100)
		(descr "USB Type-C 24P male plug, XUNPU TYPEC-950-ARP24, LCSC C2895017. Riveted clamp-plate with harpoon legs; REQUIRES 0.80 +/- 0.05 mm board. Origin is the 9.20 mm shoulder edge, board at +Y, connector body at -Y. Datasheet-exact off the archived drawing rev A 20230506 (hardware/C2895017.pdf, RECOMMENDED PCB LAYOUT view): signal 0.25 x 1.30 on 0.50 pitch, 5.50 span, spanning y = 0 .. 1.30; harpoons 0.60 x 1.55 at x = +/-3.40, spanning y = 0.20 .. 1.75, i.e. INBOARD of the signal pads. A1 at -X on the front face, at the same x as the cart receptacle's A1 (A1 at +X reversed every conductor, measured 2026-09-09); B(n) behind A(13-n). Dwgs.User carries the recommended outline: 9.20 shoulders with a 7.30 x 0.85 tab, tip corners chamfered 0.25 to clear the 6.84 cavity.")
		(tags "usb type-c plug male straddle clamp 24p xunpu")
